490	/// Imported LUTs' lattices (spec §11 GR-8): a LUT look's `.cube` file read
491	/// through `MediaImporter.readLUT` and uploaded as an `rgba16Float` `size³`
492	/// 3D texture, alpha 1 and every value clamped to 0–1, which step 4d samples
493	/// at `texture(2)` exactly as it samples a built-in look's bake.
494	///
495	/// Kept in a least-recently-used cache of `capacity`, keyed by the file's
496	/// path, byte size and modification date — so a LUT changed on disk is read
497	/// again at the next frame drawn — with a file that cannot be read or
498	/// uploaded cached as a failure under its key, so a refused or broken file
499	/// is not re-read every frame (a missing file has no key and answers nil at
500	/// once). The attributes are read through `FileManager` each time, never
501	/// through `URL.resourceValues`, which caches them on the URL. One lock, as
502	/// `LookTextures`' cache has: the preview's and an export's compositors
503	/// render on their own queues.
504	final class LutTextures {
505	    static let capacity = 8
506	
507	    private struct Key: Hashable {
508	        let path: String
509	        let size: Int
510	        let modified: Date
511	    }
