== set_video
Changes the clips' BASE video properties — position, scale, rotation, opacity, crop, corner radius, shadow, colour, chroma key, filters, reflection, spotlight and motion (what the clip does on its way in, on its way out and all the way through). The patch MERGES AT EVERY DEPTH: keys you leave out keep their values, inside a nested object too — a patch of just {shadow: {blur: 20}} keeps the shadow's colour, angle and distance — and shadow, chroma, reflection, spotlight or motion set to null clears it. A LIST is the exception: filters and obscure each replace whole, so send the whole stack and [] to clear it. A key or a value the vocabulary does not have is an error naming its dotted path (array indices included) and the value you sent; nothing is dropped, corrected or clamped. Placement is spec §5.3: the source rectangle is centred at the canvas centre plus (x, y), scaled, then rotated about that centre, and crop removes edges in place without shifting the content. To animate a property instead, add_action and then set_action_end. On an adjustment clip only color, wheels, curves, look, the point filters and opacity (the grade's strength) do anything, the qualifier narrows which pixels they reach, and blur, sharpen, pixelate or a blend mode is an error. cutout (Remove Background) is taken by media and still clips only, and behind_subject (Text Behind Subject) by any drawing clip but an adjustment or nest clip.
